<h2>The pieces this app uses</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Cloudflare product</th><th>In plain words</th><th>Used for</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Workers</td><td>your JavaScript, run on demand in every data centre</td><td>the API, sign-in, the monitor</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Workers Static Assets</td><td>files uploaded with the Worker and served for free</td><td>the web page, these guides</td></tr>
  <tr><td>D1</td><td>a SQL database (SQLite) managed by Cloudflare</td><td>users, sessions, encrypted tokens, history</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Cron Triggers</td><td>run the Worker on a schedule</td><td>JARVIS checks every minute</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Secrets and variables</td><td>settings given to the Worker; secrets are encrypted and hidden</td><td>keys, client id, origin</td></tr>
  <tr><td>workers.dev</td><td>a free web address for your Worker</td><td><code>jira-bug-dashboard-cloud.shouryacode2021.workers.dev</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Observability / tail</td><td>logs of each request and run</td><td>debugging, verifying the privacy report</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Your account, organised</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account</strong>: everything belongs to an account (yours has an account id like <code>87d5ce15…</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Workers &amp; Pages</strong>: each Worker has a name, versions (every deploy is a version), triggers (routes, cron), settings (variables, secrets, bindings) and metrics.</li>
  <li><strong>D1</strong>: each database has a name, an id, a region and a console where you can run SQL.</li>
  <li><strong>Zones</strong> (domains): only needed if you use your own domain name. With workers.dev you do not need one.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why Cloudflare for this project</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Free tier that never sleeps</strong>: other free hosts pause idle apps, which would stop background monitoring.</li>
  <li><strong>Cron included</strong>: no separate scheduler service.</li>
  <li><strong>A database included</strong>: D1, with free daily allowances.</li>
  <li><strong>Global and fast</strong>: the page is served from the data centre nearest each user.</li>
  <li><strong>One tool</strong>: Wrangler does local development, databases, secrets, deploys and logs.</li>
</ul>
<p>Next: <a href="cf-workers.html">Workers: how your code runs</a>.</p>
